# "body" t_ry< "handler" (ER4) runs the body under a trap; the handler
# sees the error as e and answers with the outcome macros. The body
# and the handler are written as lambda bodies (statements).
== SOURCE
"p_rint! 1; \"io\" []S_IGNAL \"gone\"" t_ry< "p_rint! []E_CODE e; @ r_ecover< \"0\""
== EXPAND
'{ @ -> p_rint! 1; "io" []S_IGNAL "gone" } []T_RAP '{ e -> p_rint! []E_CODE e; []R_ECOVER (0) }
== RESULT
1
io
0
